"<strong>Q8.</strong> In <strong>Self inductance</strong> the air core solenoid has N = {#} turns, ℓ = {#} cm and r = {#} cm, and the current ramps from {#} to {#} A in {#} s. (a) Find L, the field inside and the flux linkage at {#} A. (b) Find the back EMF during the ramp up, while the current is held, and during the ramp down; which way does it point each time? (c) How much energy is stored at {#} A? Check it with the energy density B²/({#}μ₀). (d) <strong>Switch off</strong> takes the current from {#} A to zero in {#} ms. What is ε, and why does a real switch spark?",
"<strong>\"A strong magnet inside a coil makes a current.\"</strong> Only a changing flux does.",
