"The magnet is a uniformly magnetized cylinder ({#} cm × {#} cm); its field and flux are computed exactly. The coil is short and its self inductance is neglected. The magnet moves as you move it: the induced force is shown but does not slow it. Field lines are {#} µWb apart.",
"Generator: uniform field, ω fixed by the motor. Sliding bar: frictionless rails, R is the whole circuit; let go, v = v₀e^(−t/τ), τ = mR/(B²L²).",
"Two coils: coaxial air coils of {#} mm copper wire. M is Maxwell's exact formula for coaxial rings averaged over both winding cross sections; L is Maxwell's formula for a coil of circular cross section, L = μ₀N²a[({#} + c²/8a²) ln(8a/c) − {#}/{#} + c²/24a²] (Rosa and Grover; Grover {#}). The coupled circuit equations are solved exactly (matrix exponential for the transient plus the phasor steady state). The EMF from moving the coil, I dM/dt, is left out.",
